§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a target-agnostic emit-framework ← pluggable backends
  b typed-AST + IR both viable sources ← per-target choice
  c round-trip invariance per-target ← emit → re-parse → compare
  d streaming-emit ← large-files handled without full-buffer
  e cert-signed output ← Ed25519 audit-chain (R16 anchor)
  f deterministic output ← byte-stable across-runs
  g source-map preservation ← location-info threaded through emission
  h incremental-emit ← skip-unchanged (build-cache)
  i target-capability declarations ← backend declares what-it-supports

§§ TARGETS
  T28.1 : CSSLv3-MIR export ← primary integration-path
    format : MLIR-like textual (matches CSSLv3 spec §§ 15)
    consumer : CSSLv3-compiler via cssllint-JSON-equivalent
    ops-mapping : cslv3.* → cssl.* per bridge-spec
    emit-what : full typed-IR + refinement-proofs + morpheme-tags
  T28.2 : Markdown export ← documentation
    format : GFM + ruby-annotations for glyphs
    use : spec-files → rendered docs-site
    emit-what : §-structure + code-blocks + tables + refs
  T28.3 : HTML export ← web-rendered
    format : semantic HTML5 + CSS-class-per-token-kind
    use : spec-viewer • hover-from-client • standalone-docs
    emit-what : syntax-highlighted + clickable cross-refs + TOC
  T28.4 : LaTeX export ← academic papers + spec-PDFs
    format : article-class + listings-package + unicode-math
    use : spec-PDFs • paper-submission
    emit-what : sectioned + math-rendered + glyph-macros
  T28.5 : JSON export ← generic tooling
    format : schema-versioned canonical-JSON
    use : third-party consumers
    emit-what : AST + types + IR all-schema-declared

§§ FILES-NEW
  parser/emit.odin                      ~600-LOC  target-agnostic framework
    Emitter interface { target, config, write, close }
    EmitContext { ast, typed, ir, source-map, stats }
    emit_module(ctx, target) → bytes + cert
    cert-signing via existing smt_audit Ed25519 infra
  parser/emit_mir.odin                  ~700-LOC  CSSLv3-MIR backend
    walk IR → MLIR-dialect textual
    op-name mapping table (cslv3.* → cssl.*)
    type-surface translation (CSLv3 types → CSSLv3 types)
    attr-preservation : morphemes + refinements + effect-rows
  parser/emit_markdown.odin             ~500-LOC  Markdown backend
    § → ## headings
    glyph-tables → Markdown-tables
    CSL-code-blocks → fenced ```csl
    ruby-annotations for-unicode-heavy lines (accessibility)
    cross-refs → [text](#anchor) auto-generated
  parser/emit_html.odin                 ~600-LOC  HTML backend
    semantic HTML5 : <section> per-§ + <code class="csl-<kind>">
    CSS-class taxonomy per-token-kind (74-glyphs + morphemes)
    TOC sidebar + cross-ref hover-preview
    standalone template or embeddable-fragment mode
  parser/emit_latex.odin                ~500-LOC  LaTeX backend
    \section per-§ + listings-lang=csl
    unicode-math macros for glyphs (≤ → \leq etc.)
    morpheme → \textsubscript{'d} style
    refinement → {v : T \mid \phi} math-rendered
  parser/emit_json.odin                 ~400-LOC  canonical JSON
    schema-versioned (schema-url + schema-version fields)
    AST + types + IR all-embedded
    stable key-ordering for diff-friendliness
    superset of existing --json flags (unified contract)
  parser/emit_schema/                   directory (schemas)
    mir-v1.json       CSSLv3-MIR JSON-schema
    markdown-v1.md    style-guide + templates
    html-v1.css       CSS taxonomy + theme
    latex-v1.sty      LaTeX style-file
    json-v1.schema    unified JSON-schema
  parser/emit_source_map.odin           ~300-LOC  source-map threading
    per-target source-map format (v3-sourcemap-standard for HTML)
    preserve line/col through emission
    enables reverse-lookup (rendered-position → original)
  parser/emit_cache.odin                ~300-LOC  incremental-emit cache
    key : (source-hash, target, config-hash)
    value : (bytes + cert + timestamp)
    skip-re-emit if hash-match
    LRU-eviction 50MB default
  tests/test_emit.odin                  ~300-LOC  Odin unit tests
  tests/test_emit_integration.py        ~500-LOC  integration
    per-target : eval/*.csl → emit → validate
    MIR : parse-back-via-CSSLv3-equivalent schema-checker
    Markdown : render via pandoc + diff golden
    HTML : parse-via-html5lib + validate
    LaTeX : compile via latexmk (CI-optional)
    JSON : schema-validate via jsonschema
  tests/emit_golden/                    per-corpus per-target golden-files
    7 corpus × 5 targets = 35 goldens
  scripts/check_emit_cert.py            verify Ed25519 cert-chain

§§ CLI-SURFACE
  parser --emit=mir <file>         → CSSLv3-MIR textual
  parser --emit=markdown <file>    → Markdown
  parser --emit=html <file>        → HTML5
  parser --emit=latex <file>       → LaTeX
  parser --emit=json <file>        → canonical JSON
  parser --emit=X --out=<path>     → write to file (cert sidecar)
  parser --emit=X --sign           → cert-sign via Ed25519 audit
  parser --emit=X --incremental    → use emit-cache
  parser --emit-selftest           → run per-target selftest
  parser --emit=X --schema         → print target schema
  parser --emit=X --no-source-map  → disable source-map embedding

§§ SEVERITY-INTEGRATION
  emit-failed-verification    : always-E
  target-capability-missing   : always-E (request-op not-supported)
  cert-signing-failed         : always-E
  source-map-drop             : W@default • E@strict
  incomplete-emit (fallback)  : W@default • E@strict
  diagnostic-codes : CSL-E-600..699 (emit) + CSL-W-600..699

§§ ROUND-TRIP INVARIANTS (per-target)
  MIR      : emit → external-parser-stub → schema-equiv
  Markdown : emit → parse → structural-equiv (section-tree)
  HTML     : emit → html5lib-parse → DOM-equiv
  LaTeX    : emit → compile → PDF-produced (CI-optional)
  JSON     : emit → parse → AST-shape-equiv (strict)
  golden-diff per-target + CI-gate

