═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ T28-depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Emission architectures :
    visitor : per-node-kind dispatch • classic • recommend
    pipeline : transform-chain • MLIR-style • heavier
    monolithic : single-switch • simple • poor-extensibility
    recommend visitor ∵ matches pprint + ir_print precedent
  Round-trip strategies :
    syntactic : emit → parse → source-equiv (strict)
    structural : emit → parse → AST-equiv (relaxed)
    semantic : emit → parse → type-equiv (loose)
    recommend structural per-target ∵ matches T12 RT-invariant
  Source-map formats :
    v3 sourcemap (JSON) : web-standard • VLQ-encoded
    inline : per-output-line mapping comment
    sidecar : .map file alongside output
    recommend sidecar + v3 format ∵ tool-compat
  Schema versioning :
    semver-independent per-schema
    forward-compat via "schemaVersion" field
    consumer-detects + adapts
  Certificate signing :
    existing smt_audit Ed25519 reusable
    emit-cert schema : (hash, target, version, signature, timestamp)
    chain = audit-chain extension
  Incremental-emit cache :
    key = BLAKE3(source + target + config)
    value = bytes + cert + size
    LRU + disk-backed (.emit-cache/)
  Markdown-for-CSL notes :
    ruby-annotations aid accessibility (screen-readers for glyphs)
    fenced-code-blocks preserve glyphs raw
    cross-refs : auto-generate anchors from §-headings

